423
00:17:40,340 --> 00:17:43,260
There are many meanings of the word efficiency.

424
00:17:43,260 --> 00:17:45,380
So there's one that normal people use

425
00:17:45,380 --> 00:17:47,740
that you get out of the dictionary,

426
00:17:47,740 --> 00:17:49,380
which is that efficiency is something like,

427
00:17:49,380 --> 00:17:51,620
quote, effective operations measured by a comparison

428
00:17:51,620 --> 00:17:54,620
of production with cost as an energy time and money,

429
00:17:54,620 --> 00:17:56,900
like a fuel-efficient vehicle.

430
00:17:56,900 --> 00:17:58,580
All right, so fuel-efficient vehicle means

431
00:17:58,580 --> 00:18:01,220
you get a lot of miles per gallon out of it.

432
00:18:01,220 --> 00:18:04,180
That is a definition of efficiency,

433
00:18:04,180 --> 00:18:07,460
and economists, once in a while, do use efficiency

434
00:18:07,460 --> 00:18:10,020
in this dictionary sense, such as the ratio

435
00:18:10,020 --> 00:18:13,300
of the value of output to input, something like that.

436
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:16,020
But normally, economists use the word efficiency

437
00:18:16,020 --> 00:18:17,900
in totally different ways that have nothing to do

438
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:21,380
with this verbal definition, and then the really bad part

439
00:18:21,380 --> 00:18:23,260
is economists will often equivocate,

440
00:18:23,260 --> 00:18:26,000
which means they will use multiple definitions

441
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,220
in the same essay or the same page,

442
00:18:28,220 --> 00:18:30,540
the same paragraph, the same sentence,

443
00:18:30,540 --> 00:18:34,340
and then what are we to do other than say, stop,

444
00:18:34,340 --> 00:18:37,620
you have used the same word in two different sentences

445
00:18:37,620 --> 00:18:40,660
in a single sentence without appearing

446
00:18:40,660 --> 00:18:42,660
to have any idea what you're doing.

447
00:18:42,660 --> 00:18:44,540
All right, so the two most common uses

448
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:47,660
of efficiency in economics are, first of all,

449
00:18:47,660 --> 00:18:49,500
parade efficiency, and second of all,

